            <div xml:id="d401">

                <pb facs="0558" n="446" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg446"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/7440: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-11-27T10:00:00+08:00">November 27, 1935—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 27—6:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>179. Three hundred and fifteen Japanese infantry troops have arrived in Peiping
                    during the past 2 days and are billeted at the Japanese Club which is in the
                    city outside of the Legation quarter. (The regular Japanese garrison numbers 321
                    and is billeted in the Japanese Embassy guard.) The new arrivals are without
                    special equipment.</p>
                <p>2. Reliable information has just been received that a Japanese troop train of 17
                    cars passed through Shanhaikwan this morning from the north, destination at
                    present unknown.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Nanking and Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
